    <string name="privacy_dialog_title">OptiLens privacy policy</string>
    <string name="privacy_dialog_body">Your photos stay on your device\nCapture, processing, enhancement and editing all run locally on your phone. OptiLens does not upload your photos.\n\nPermissions\n• Camera: used only for the viewfinder and taking photos.\n• Photos: saved to DCIM/OptiLens with scoped storage; the system Photo Picker is used to open other photos, so no broad storage permission is requested.\n• Location: not used. OptiLens photos are saved without GPS coordinates; an enhanced copy of another photo keeps its location only if the original already had it.\n\nAds\nThe free version may show a banner in the gallery from Google Mobile Ads, which may collect device identifiers under Google\'s own policies. Whether ads run and which ad units are used comes from our configuration service (WAPCentral); fetching it sends only the app\'s identifier, never photos or personal data. Ads never appear in the camera viewfinder and never block capturing, enhancing or saving. Pro removes ads.\n\nDiagnostics\nOptiLens does not currently send analytics or crash reports anywhere.\n\nCache\nTemporary files and thumbnails can be cleared at any time from this Settings screen.</string>
